    "notes_unique": "Nan Madol (megalithic basalt city on Pohnpei, ~92 artificial islets on coral reef, built 1200-1500 CE by Saudeleur dynasty, 750k tons of basalt columns transported, 'Venice of the Pacific', UNESCO 2016, how stones moved remains mystery, spiritual centre of Pohnpei); Chuuk Lagoon/Ghost Fleet (Truk Lagoon, WWII Japanese naval base, Operation Hailstone Feb 1944 US air attack destroyed 12 warships/32 merchant ships/249 aircraft, now world's greatest wreck diving site, 60+ ships, oil still leaking environmental concern); Yapese stone money (rai, massive limestone discs quarried from Palau 400km away, transported by canoe, oral history records ownership, not physically moved when traded, parallels to modern cryptocurrency cited); Compact of Free Association (COFA, 1986 renewed 2023, US provides funding/defence, FSM citizens can live/work in US freely, ~40k in US, strategic denial of area to other powers, Pacific pivot importance); 607 islands across 2,700km of ocean (four states: Yap, Chuuk, Pohnpei, Kosrae, extreme diversity, different languages, distinct cultures, fragile federation); traditional navigation (Carolinian navigators, star compass, wave reading, bird flight, no instruments, UNESCO, Mau Piailug taught Hawaiian canoe revival); betel nut (areca nut, universal social custom, red teeth); depopulation (emigration to US, brain drain, population declining); federation fragility (Chuuk secession discussions periodic); climate change (atolls vulnerable, sea level rise, freshwater lens contamination)",
